    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Army signed a $25 million contract in January 1942 to build a training camp on 56,000 acres north of Bastrop, Texas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Swift%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Construction of Camp Swift was completed in just 108 working days, a record pace for a 56,000‑acre military installation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Swift%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During World War II, German prisoners of war arrived in large numbers, peaking at about 10,000 on the camp’s grounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Swift%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Camp Swift’s 95th, 97th, and 102nd Infantry Divisions, the 10th Mountain Division, and several tank destroyer battalions trained there during the war.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
